# MAGIC %md-sandbox
# MAGIC # Lecture - Introduction to Genie Agents
# MAGIC
# MAGIC ## Overview
# MAGIC
# MAGIC A **Genie Agent** is a curated, natural language interface to a domain's Unity Catalog data, enabling business users to interact with that data using plain English. It uses generative AI tailored to your organization's data and terminology, and it can be continuously improved through monitoring and user feedback.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Rather than requiring business users to ask data analysts for help, Genie Agents allow anyone to ask questions in plain English and receive SQL-backed answers, tables, and visualizations, all grounded in governed Unity Catalog data.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC In this lecture, you will quickly review the components of the Databricks AI/BI product family:
# MAGIC
# MAGIC - AI/BI Dashboards
# MAGIC - Genie Agents
# MAGIC - Genie One *(formerly Databricks One)*
# MAGIC - Genie Code
# MAGIC
# MAGIC You will learn how they complement each other, then focus on how a Genie Agent translates a natural language question into a SQL result, understand the components that make up a Genie Agent, and consider the common challenges that arise when building one without additional configuration.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC ## Learning Objectives
# MAGIC
# MAGIC By the end of this lecture, you will be able to:
# MAGIC
# MAGIC 1. **Describe the Databricks AI/BI product family** and explain the difference between them.
# MAGIC 2. **Explain how a Genie Agent translates a natural language question into a SQL result**, including the five-step process from question to answer.
# MAGIC 3. **Identify and describe the six components of a Genie Agent**: Unity Catalog tables, SQL logic (joins, expressions, example queries), text instructions, common questions, table/column metadata, and benchmarks.
# MAGIC 4. **Recognize common challenges in Genie Agent configuration** like misunderstood business jargon, incorrect table or column usage, and opaque column values.

