# MAGIC %md-sandbox
# MAGIC ##### EXPAND FOR ADDITIONAL NOTES
# MAGIC
# MAGIC <details>
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Databricks AI/BI is a product family that brings intelligence to business analytics. It includes four complementary tools:
# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### AI/BI Dashboards
# MAGIC Dashboards are the traditional BI experience.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Analysts build curated visualizations, charts, and reports that stakeholders consume. Dashboards are great when you know exactly what questions need to be answered and want to present that data in a polished, repeatable format.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### Genie Agents
# MAGIC Genie Agents take the opposite approach. Instead of pre-building answers, a Genie Agent lets business users **ask their own questions** in plain English. The agent interprets the question, generates SQL, runs it against your Unity Catalog tables, and returns the result.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC All without the user needing to know SQL.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### Genie One
# MAGIC Genie is a user interface designed for business users, giving them a single, intuitive entry point to interact with data and AI in Databricks, without needing to navigate technical concepts such as compute, queries, models, or notebooks.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### Genie Code
# MAGIC Genie Code is the AI assistant for builders. It lives inside notebooks, Apache Spark Declarative pipelines, the SQL editor, and the dashboard editor, helping data engineers, analysts, and data scientists write, debug, and iterate on code.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### How They Work Together
# MAGIC - **Dashboards** answer the questions you **know** your business will ask repeatedly.
# MAGIC - **Genie Agents** answer the questions that come up **on the fly**. Ad-hoc questions that no one anticipated when designing the dashboard.
# MAGIC - **Genie** fills in the gaps between tools and people by bringing your data, dashboards, and AI assistants into one place, so everyone can find, understand, and act on insights in their daily work.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Together, they give organizations both curated insights and self-service exploration on the same governed data.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC </details>
# MAGIC

