# MAGIC   <b>How does Genie generate a response?</b>
# MAGIC   &nbsp;<a href="https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/genie-agents/concepts" style="color: #1B5162;">AWS</a>
# MAGIC   &nbsp;<a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/databricks/genie-agents/concepts" style="color: #1B5162;">Azure</a>
# MAGIC   &nbsp;<a href="https://docs.databricks.com/gcp/en/genie-agents/concepts" style="color: #1B5162;">GCP</a>
# MAGIC </div>
# MAGIC
# MAGIC </div>

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md-sandbox
# MAGIC ##### EXPAND FOR ADDITIONAL NOTES
# MAGIC
# MAGIC <details>
# MAGIC
# MAGIC High-level Genie Agent overview.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### 1. User Asks a Question
# MAGIC The user types a question in plain English into the Genie Agent chat interface. No SQL knowledge is required.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Questions can range from:
# MAGIC
# MAGIC - Simple: "How many customers do we have?"
# MAGIC - Complex: "What are the top 5 franchise locations by revenue in Japan?"
# MAGIC
# MAGIC
# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### 2. Genie Selects Relevant Context
# MAGIC Genie does not just "read everything". It selects the most relevant context to understand the question.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC This can include:
# MAGIC
# MAGIC - **Table schemas** — column names and data types from Unity Catalog tables
# MAGIC - **Column and table descriptions** — metadata explaining what fields represent
# MAGIC - **SQL logic** — joins, expressions, and example queries that encode business definitions
# MAGIC - **Instructions** — guidance for behavior, edge cases, and business rules
# MAGIC - **Example questions** — natural language to SQL patterns
# MAGIC - **Conversation history** — prior questions in the same thread
# MAGIC
# MAGIC The better this context is curated, the more accurate the Genie Agent becomes.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC
# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### 3. SQL Is Generated
# MAGIC Based on the selected context, Genie generates a **read-only SQL query**.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC - The SQL reflects both the user question and the curated data model
# MAGIC - It is fully visible to the user, there is no black box
# MAGIC - In some cases, Genie may reuse trusted or predefined SQL logic
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Users can review the SQL to validate correctness.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC
# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### 4. SQL Is Executed
# MAGIC The generated SQL runs on the Genie Agents's configured SQL warehouse.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC - Handles scale and concurrency automatically
# MAGIC - Uses the same execution engine as Databricks SQL
# MAGIC - Returns structured results from governed data
# MAGIC
# MAGIC
# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### 5. Response Is Returned
# MAGIC - Results are displayed as a table, often with a short summary
# MAGIC - The generated SQL is shown for transparency
# MAGIC - Users can provide feedback (thumbs up/down)
# MAGIC - Follow-up questions can be asked in the same conversation
# MAGIC
# MAGIC If Genie cannot confidently answer, it may first ask a **clarifying question** before generating SQL.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC </details>

