# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### Genie Agents
# MAGIC
# MAGIC - Designed for **business users and analysts** who need answers from data without writing SQL or Python.
# MAGIC - Built around **curated Unity Catalog data**. Built by admins and data teams set up the "room" with governed tables, descriptions, and example questions.
# MAGIC - The experience is a natural language chat interface where users ask, the agent generates SQL, results appear.
# MAGIC - The key word is **curated**. Genie Agents work best when someone has intentionally prepared the data room for the audience.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### Genie Code
# MAGIC
# MAGIC - Designed for **builders** like data engineers, analytics engineers, data scientists.
# MAGIC - Lives **inside the Databricks platform itself** as an assistant panel visible in notebooks, SQL editor, Apache Spark Declarative Pipelines, dashboards.
# MAGIC - Can write code, explain code, debug errors, and suggest next steps autonomously.
# MAGIC - Think of it as a pair programmer embedded directly into the tools builders already use.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC #### Summary: Why This Distinction Matters
# MAGIC
# MAGIC - **Genie Agents** is for business users asking questions of their data.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC - **Genie Code** is for developers building and operating data workflows. We're focused on Genie Agents in this course.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC </details>

